# Git LFS — large binary ML artifacts (audit finding L-1).
#
# The .pkl model files are ~113 MB total (cyberguard_rf_final.pkl 49 MB,
# network_attack_model.pkl 54 MB) and have been re-committed as plain blobs
# across several "Update data science models" revisions, bloating every clone.
#
# One-time per clone / CI runner:
#     git lfs install
#
# To move the artifacts ALREADY in history from plain blobs into LFS — this
# REWRITES history, so coordinate with everyone and force-push once:
#     git lfs migrate import --include="*.pkl,*.joblib" --everything
#     # then:  git reflog expire --expire=now --all && git gc --prune=now --aggressive
#
# New / changed .pkl files are stored in LFS automatically once git-lfs is
# installed and this file is in place.
*.pkl     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.joblib  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Treat model metadata as text so it stays diff-able.
*.json    text eol=lf
